00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:51.000
The grief that Maya felt was enormous. Her plan for her life, her very identity, had been wrapped around music. She didn't know what to do next. And then one day, as she was helping her parents clean out their basement, she stumbled on one of her sister's course books. It was The Language Instinct by Stephen Pinker. And as she read the book, Maya found herself captivated by the human mind. She realized she wanted to learn more about the brain and how it works, and so she decided to study cognitive science. Fast forward a couple of decades, and Maya

