has since completed a Rhodes Scholarship, and a stint in the Obama White House. I tell you Maya's story not to suggest it should be your story, but because it shows that when the world is uncertain and the ground under our feet feels unsteady, that's often the time we discover new things about ourselves. Periods of disruption invariably lead to invention and reinvention. A number of years ago, there was a transit strike in London. Many subway stations were closed. People had to find a new way to get around. It was stressful.

