00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:47.000
life. Like Maya Shankar, you have suddenly seen your plans upended. The way forward is unclear. But what lies before you is an opportunity to look at the world with fresh eyes. I'm often reminded of this when I travel to a new city. I'm peering around, looking with fascination at the buildings, the parks. Meanwhile, all around me, the people who actually live in that city are hurrying about, barely looking up, not stopping to notice the sites around them. When chaos strikes, we all become tourists in our own lives. We start to see with fresh eyes, and when we do, we realize the world really does have endless possibilities. In fact, this is why we have rights of passage like graduation ceremonies. They are designed to give us a chance to stop, to take stock,

